<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico completes money market operation.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico completes money market operation.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico completed all three direct sales of paper and three repurchase agreements whereby it had sought to drain 1.551 billion pesos from the secondary money market on Wednesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    344 days   21.78 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    176 days   21.30 pct</p>
<p>    150 million     85 days   20.98 pct</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were placed as follows:</p>
<p>    450 million     35 days   21.36 pct</p>
<p>    500 million     27 days   21.70 pct</p>
<p>    151 million	1 day    20.89 pct</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( -- Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
